.TH GET 1 "2026-09-23" "get 4.0.0" "User Commands"
.
.SH NAME
get \- get anything from your computer
.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B get
.RI \(dq query \(dq
.RI [ flags ]
.br
.B get set
.I option
.RI [ value ]
.br
.B get config
.RI [ \-\-reset | \-\- option ]
.br
.B get cache
.RI [ \-\-clean | "\-\-unset \(dq" query \(dq ]
.br
.B get log
.RI [ \-\-clean ]
.br
.B get get
.RI [ \-\-name | \-\-intro | \-\-version | \-\-author | \-\-license | \-\-github ]
.br
.B get version
.br
.B get \-\-version
.br
.B get \-V
.br
.B get isok
.br
.B get help
.
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B get
sends a natural-language query to an OpenAI-compatible model and reads local
facts on its behalf. It is a query tool: it doesn't change the system.
.PP
The model receives typed readers (environment, files, search, processes, Git
status/diff) and answers from what they return. Tool calls are sent as native
function calling, falling back to structured JSON when the provider rejects
them. A query that explicitly asks for "no tools" is routed as text-only:
no tools are offered and nothing is executed.
.PP
Every proposed, revised, or cached command passes the same mandatory read-only
policy before it runs. Optional extras \(em a supplemental regex
.RI ( command\-pattern ),
a second model review
.RI ( double\-check ),
or per-command confirmation
.RI ( manual\-confirm )
\(em layer on top of it. All are off by default.
.
.SH HARNESS
The harness controls how evidence is gathered:
.TP
.B auto
Default. Look around, then answer; a denied command is skipped and the model
may pick another reader within the inspection budget.
.TP
.B direct
One model turn, at most one tool call.
.TP
.B loop
Serial observe-and-refine for dependent multi-step work.
.TP
.B parallel
Independent read-only calls run concurrently, up to
.BR max\-parallel .
.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS "Query (default)"
.BI "get \(dq" query "\(dq [" flags "]"
.RS
Runs the query with the configured harness.
.RE
.SS set
.BI "get set " option " [" value ]
.RS
Sets one persistent option. Omitting the value resets it to the default.
.RE
.SS config
.B get config
.RS
Shows settings; the API key is reported only as set or not set.
.B \-\-reset
restores defaults and removes the stored key;
.BI \-\- option
shows one setting.
.RE
.SS cache
.B get cache
.RS
Shows cache counts, limits, and file location.
.B \-\-clean
removes all entries;
.BI "\-\-unset \(dq" query \(dq
removes entries matching the query text.
.RE
.SS log
.B get log
.RS
Shows log status and location.
.B \-\-clean
removes all entries.
.RE
.SS get
.B get get
.RS
Shows application metadata:
.BR \-\-name ", " \-\-intro ", " \-\-version ", " \-\-author ", " \-\-license ", " \-\-github .
.RE
.SS version
.BR "get version" ", " "get \-\-version" ", " "get \-V"
.RS
Shows the version. Doesn't require provider configuration.
.RE
.SS isok
.B get isok
.RS
Checks key, URL, and model with a minimal provider request.
.RE
.
.SH QUERY FLAGS
.TP
.B \-\-cache / \-\-no\-cache
Force (or bypass) cache use. \fB\-\-cache\fR may also store a final text answer
when no reusable command exists.
.TP
.B \-\-manual\-confirm / \-\-no\-manual\-confirm
Prompt before every command (or don't).
.TP
.B \-\-double\-check / \-\-no\-double\-check
Add a second model safety review. The mandatory policy runs either way.
.TP
.BI \-\-harness " kind"
auto, direct, loop, or parallel for this query.
.TP
.BI \-\-protocol " kind"
auto, native, or json tool encoding for this query.
.TP
.B \-\-instance / \-\-no\-instance
Aliases for direct / loop.
.TP
.B \-\-hide\-process / \-\-no\-hide\-process
Suppress (or show) progress and intermediate observations.
.TP
.B \-\-system\-proxy / \-\-no\-system\-proxy
Prefer Windows Internet Settings over terminal proxy variables.
.TP
.B \-\-vivid / \-\-no\-vivid
ANSI styling on or off.
.TP
.B \-\-markdown / \-\-no\-markdown
Render the model's Markdown in an interactive terminal, or show the source.
.TP
.BI \-\-model " name"
Override the model for this query.
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " seconds"
Override the API request timeout.
.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "key " string
API key. Stored as a 0600 file on Linux, DPAPI-protected on Windows. Not
printed or logged. Default: empty.
.TP
.BI "url " URL
API base URL. Default: https://api.deepseek.com.
.TP
.BI "model " string
Model identifier. Default: deepseek-flash (DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash).
.TP
.BI "manual\-confirm " bool
Confirm each command interactively. Default: false.
.TP
.BI "double\-check " bool
Add a second model safety review. Default: false.
.TP
.BI "harness " kind
auto, direct, loop, or parallel. Default: auto.
.TP
.BI "tool\-protocol " kind
auto, native, or json. Default: auto (native with JSON fallback).
.TP
.BI "timeout " "int | false"
API timeout in seconds. Default: 300.
.TP
.BI "max\-token " "int | false"
Maximum response tokens. Default: 20480.
.TP
.BI "max\-rounds " int
Inspection-turn limit; one final answer turn is separate. Default: 6.
.TP
.BI "max\-tool\-calls " int
Tool-start limit per query. Default: 16.
.TP
.BI "max\-parallel " int
Maximum concurrent tool calls. Default: 4.
.TP
.BI "query\-timeout " int
Whole-query deadline in seconds, model and tools included. Default: 120.
.TP
.BI "diagnostics " bool
Structured query events and counters on stderr. Default: false.
.TP
.BI "command\-timeout " int
Hard deadline per command in seconds. Default: 30.
.TP
.BI "max\-output\-bytes " int
Captured bytes per command. Default: 1048576.
.TP
.BI "command\-pattern " regex
Extra forbidden-command regex. Omit the value to restore the built-in
semantic-only policy. Default: off.
.TP
.BI "system\-prompt " string
Additional model instruction. Default: empty.
.TP
.BI "shell " string
Shell executable. Default: bash on Unix, powershell on Windows.
.TP
.BI "log " bool
Execution logging. Default: true.
.TP
.BI "hide\-process " bool
Suppress progress and intermediate output. Default: false.
.TP
.BI "system\-proxy " bool
Prefer Windows Internet Settings over terminal proxy variables. Default: false.
.TP
.BI "cache " bool
Deterministic caching. Default: true.
.TP
.BI "cache\-expiry " "int | false"
Cache lifetime in days. Default: 30.
.TP
.BI "cache\-max\-entries " "int | false"
Cache entry cap. Default: 1000.
.TP
.BI "log\-max\-entries " "int | false"
Log entry cap. Default: 1000.
.TP
.BI "vivid " bool
ANSI styling and animation. Default: true.
.TP
.BI "markdown " bool
Render model answers in interactive terminals. Pipes, redirects, and
TERM=dumb keep the source text; NO_COLOR drops the colors. Default: true.
.TP
.BI "instance " bool
Alias for harness: true selects direct, false selects auto. Default: false.
.
.SH SAFETY
Typed readers (environment, files, search, processes) don't execute shell
text; missing values, empty matches, and truncated pages are reported as such.
.PP
On Linux, free-form scripts and complex shell computation run in an isolated
sandbox \(em bubblewrap namespaces, read-only host mounts, seccomp, and resource
limits \(em with no network access. If the sandbox can't be established, the
script doesn't run. macOS and Windows offer the typed readers and known host
queries, but not arbitrary computation.
.PP
Ordinary Git status/diff read a private metadata snapshot instead of the real
index; executable filters and submodules are disabled, so results can differ
slightly from interactive Git. The observation says where it came from.
.PP
This boundary guards against mutation, not disclosure: what
.B get
reads is sent to your configured provider to be answered. Environment
credential values are redacted; file contents are not passed through a
general secret filter.
.
.SH CACHE
A successful single-step query stores a typed plan, keyed by provider, model,
strategy, working directory, and related context. A hit costs zero model
calls: the command is revalidated and re-executed, so dynamic answers stay
current. Multi-step results are not cached, and a text-only query doesn't
execute a cached command.
.PP
Cache writes are locked across processes; the file is atomically replaced with
a last-good backup.
.
.SH NETWORK
All model traffic uses one TLS-verifying HTTP client, including through
proxies; requests carrying credentials don't follow redirects. On Windows,
the native ROOT certificate store is used, so no separate CA bundle is
needed.
.PP
Terminal proxy variables are honored by default; with system-proxy=true,
enabled Windows Internet Settings take precedence. NO_PROXY takes
comma-separated domains (matching subdomains), IP literals, and \fI*\fR, with
optional ports (example.com:443); IPv6 ports use brackets ([::1]:8080).
.
.SH INSTALL
Download a release and keep its files together. Either way leaves an
existing configuration in place. With Python, run
\fBpython get_ready.py\fR
to check the package, copy the program, and update PATH. A first install
then offers presets for DeepSeek, MiMo, GLM, Kimi, GPT, Claude, Qwen, Grok,
Gemini, MiniMax, and Ollama, or any OpenAI-compatible endpoint. Then run
\fBget version\fR.
Without Python, copy the file yourself and put its directory on PATH.
Linux \fIget-linux-x64\fR and macOS \fIget-macos-arm64\fR become
\fI~/.local/bin/get\fR.
Run \fBchmod +x\fR on that file. On macOS also run
\fBxattr -d com.apple.quarantine ~/.local/bin/get\fR.
Windows \fIget-windows-x64.exe\fR becomes
\fI%LOCALAPPDATA%\ePrograms\eget\eget.exe\fR
beside libcrypto-3.dll, libssl-3.dll, and zlib1.dll. The manual page is
optional: copy \fIget.1\fR to \fI~/.local/share/man/man1/get.1\fR.
.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/get/config.json
Configuration (Linux).
.TP
.I ~/.config/get/key
API key file, mode 0600 (Linux).
.TP
.I ~/.config/get/cache.json
Cache store.
.TP
.I ~/.config/get/get.log
Execution log.
.PP
On Windows these live under %APPDATA%\eget; the key is DPAPI-protected there.
The Windows release also installs the required OpenSSL runtime DLLs beside the
executable.
.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Configuration, provider, protocol, policy, or general error.
.TP
.B 124
Command deadline exceeded.
.TP
.B 126
Tool proposal rejected, with no safe revision inside the budget.
.TP
.B 130
Interrupted by Ctrl+C.
.TP
.B other
Exit status of the terminating command.
.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
get \(dqcurrent directory\(dq
get \(dqcompare disk and memory usage\(dq \-\-harness parallel
get \(dqservice status\(dq \-\-double\-check
get set tool\-protocol native
get set max\-parallel 6
get cache \-\-clean
.fi
.
